production version upload process
----------------------------------
1. merge from staging to master
2. go to master and pull 
3. change version in packet.json , commit and push to master
4. git tag -a v1.0.XXX -m "***version upload on 01.01.2021***"   3 stars means bold and italic
5. git push origin v1.0.XX
6. git push reability-prod master
7. login to heroku and run in console: npm run migrate:run
8. start tests



version numbers are in the server's packet.json file
zugi numbers are production versions like 1.0.14 and fixes are 1.0.14a or b or c - this is production hot fixes

first version to staging after a lot of changes are e-zugi meaning 1.0.15 and little fixes 1.0.15a b c....
the version number is in thelogin screen in bottomleft side




in your local computer go to the branch of the main code 


make pull make merge if needed  

run the application locally 

git push reability-staging staging:master    (meaning push from 0.11 to master in the remote)

